  "worked_solution": "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+P(x){y}^{\u2032}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{\u2032}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in standard form. Since $x>0$, we can divide both sides by ${x}^{2}+1$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}{y}^{\u2032}+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}+1}y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, the coefficient of ${y}^{\u2032}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{\u2032}(x)=-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x).\n$$",
